From 67c2011f732e9e76f5e2ad492eba861a9bd105df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 13:38:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] (be) fp-walk native stack collector

Rewrite the stub collect step as the real frame-pointer walk: interrupt each
target thread with SIGRTMIN+6 queued via SI_QUEUE carrying a per-request
sequence token, walk RIP/RBP from the ucontext into a single never-freed global
slot bounded by max_frames and max_stack_bytes, then let the shared
run_collection resolve DSOs and report signal_blocked / timeout / partial.

The handler validates the sender (si_pid) and the token on entry and re-checks
the token before publishing, so a late handler from a finished dump drops its
result. The single global slot plus the token close attempt-1's use-after-free
and late-responder windows. fp-walk uses no libunwind and overrides no
dl_iterate_phdr, so it never collides with the jemalloc allocator path.

Reference: docs/phase2-design.md "Variant Mechanics -> fp-walk";
<ck>/src/Storages/System/StorageSystemStackTrace.cpp.
---
 .../http/action/native_stack_collect.cpp      | 282 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 270 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

